  "peptideContentMelanotanIiDescription": "La melanotán II es un análogo sintético de la hormona estimulante de los alfa-melanocitos (α-MSH). Se desarrolló originalmente como posible agente para el bronceado sin sol y también se ha asociado con efectos sobre el apetito y la libido.",
  "@peptideContentMelanotanIiDescription": {
    "description": "Educational reference description for Melanotan II.",
    "sourceString": "Melanotan II is a synthetic analogue of the alpha-melanocyte-stimulating hormone (α-MSH). It was originally developed as a potential sunless tanning agent and has also been associated with appetite and libido effects.",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational reference description for Melanotan II."
  },
  "peptideContentMelanotanIiTypicalDose": "250–1000 mcg de carga, luego mantenimiento",
  "@peptideContentMelanotanIiTypicalDose": {
    "description": "Reference amount text for Melanotan II; this is not a dosing recommendation.",
    "sourceString": "250–1000 mcg loading, then maintenance",
    "sourceDescription": "Reference amount text for Melanotan II; this is not a dosing recommendation."
  },
  "peptideContentMelanotanIiHalfLife": "~1 hora",
  "@peptideContentMelanotanIiHalfLife": {
    "description": "Educational half-life reference for Melanotan II.",
    "sourceString": "~1 hour",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational half-life reference for Melanotan II."
  },
  "peptideContentMelanotanIiNotes": "No aprobado para ningún uso médico. Los efectos secundarios reportados con mayor frecuencia incluyen náuseas y oscurecimiento de lunares existentes. Cualquier lunar nuevo o que cambie debe ser evaluado por un dermatólogo.",
  "@peptideContentMelanotanIiNotes": {
    "description": "Neutral educational notes for Melanotan II; preserve non-prescriptive framing.",
    "sourceString": "Not approved for any medical use. Common reported side effects include nausea and darkening of existing moles. Any new or changing mole should be evaluated by a dermatologist.",
    "sourceDescription": "Neutral educational notes for Melanotan II; preserve non-prescriptive framing."
  },
  "peptideContentPt141Description": "PT-141, también conocido como bremelanotida y comercializado como Vyleesi, es un agonista del receptor de melanocortina aprobado por la FDA para el trastorno del deseo sexual hipoactivo en mujeres premenopáusicas. Actúa sobre vías del sistema nervioso central.",
  "@peptideContentPt141Description": {
    "description": "Educational reference description for PT-141 (Bremelanotide).",
    "sourceString": "PT-141, also known as Bremelanotide and marketed as Vyleesi, is a melanocortin receptor agonist approved by the FDA for hypoactive sexual desire disorder in premenopausal women. It acts on central nervous system pathways.",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational reference description for PT-141 (Bremelanotide)."
  },
  "peptideContentPt141TypicalDose": "1.25–1.75 mg según sea necesario",
  "@peptideContentPt141TypicalDose": {
    "description": "Reference amount text for PT-141 (Bremelanotide); this is not a dosing recommendation.",
    "sourceString": "1.25–1.75 mg as needed",
    "sourceDescription": "Reference amount text for PT-141 (Bremelanotide); this is not a dosing recommendation."
  },
  "peptideContentPt141HalfLife": "~2 horas",
  "@peptideContentPt141HalfLife": {
    "description": "Educational half-life reference for PT-141 (Bremelanotide).",
    "sourceString": "~2 hours",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational half-life reference for PT-141 (Bremelanotide)."
  },
  "peptideContentPt141Notes": "Medicamento con receta en algunos mercados. Se toma según sea necesario, no en un horario fijo. Los efectos secundarios comunes incluyen náuseas y aumentos transitorios de la presión arterial.",
  "@peptideContentPt141Notes": {
    "description": "Neutral educational notes for PT-141 (Bremelanotide); preserve non-prescriptive framing.",
    "sourceString": "Prescription medication in some markets. Taken as needed rather than on a fixed schedule. Common side effects include nausea and transient blood pressure increases.",
    "sourceDescription": "Neutral educational notes for PT-141 (Bremelanotide); preserve non-prescriptive framing."
  },
  "peptideContentDsipDescription": "El péptido inductor del sueño delta (DSIP) es un nonapéptido aislado del cerebro de conejo en la década de 1970. Se ha estudiado por su posible papel en la regulación del sueño, la modulación del dolor y la respuesta al estrés, aunque sus mecanismos siguen sin estar claros.",
  "@peptideContentDsipDescription": {
    "description": "Educational reference description for DSIP.",
    "sourceString": "Delta Sleep-Inducing Peptide (DSIP) is a nonapeptide isolated from rabbit brain in the 1970s. It has been studied for possible roles in sleep regulation, pain modulation, and stress response, though mechanisms remain unclear.",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational reference description for DSIP."
  },
  "peptideContentDsipTypicalDose": "100–500 mcg antes de dormir",
  "@peptideContentDsipTypicalDose": {
    "description": "Reference amount text for DSIP; this is not a dosing recommendation.",
    "sourceString": "100–500 mcg before bed",
    "sourceDescription": "Reference amount text for DSIP; this is not a dosing recommendation."
  },
  "peptideContentDsipHalfLife": "~7 minutos",
  "@peptideContentDsipHalfLife": {
    "description": "Educational half-life reference for DSIP.",
    "sourceString": "~7 minutes",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational half-life reference for DSIP."
  },
  "peptideContentDsipNotes": "Se administra típicamente antes de dormir. Tiene una semivida plasmática corta, aunque los efectos reportados pueden durar más. La evidencia disponible sigue siendo limitada.",
  "@peptideContentDsipNotes": {
    "description": "Neutral educational notes for DSIP; preserve non-prescriptive framing.",
    "sourceString": "Typically administered before bed. Short plasma half-life but reported effects may outlast it. Evidence base remains limited.",
    "sourceDescription": "Neutral educational notes for DSIP; preserve non-prescriptive framing."
  },
  "peptideContentThymosinAlpha1Description": "La timosina alfa-1 es un péptido de 28 aminoácidos aislado originalmente del tejido tímico. Se ha aprobado en varios países como terapia inmunomoduladora complementaria (marca Zadaxin) para la hepatitis B y C.",
  "@peptideContentThymosinAlpha1Description": {
    "description": "Educational reference description for Thymosin Alpha-1.",
    "sourceString": "Thymosin Alpha-1 is a 28-amino-acid peptide originally isolated from thymus tissue. It has been approved in multiple countries as an adjunct immune-modulating therapy (brand name Zadaxin) for hepatitis B and C.",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational reference description for Thymosin Alpha-1."
  },
  "peptideContentThymosinAlpha1TypicalDose": "1.6 mg dos veces por semana",
  "@peptideContentThymosinAlpha1TypicalDose": {
    "description": "Reference amount text for Thymosin Alpha-1; this is not a dosing recommendation.",
    "sourceString": "1.6 mg twice weekly",
    "sourceDescription": "Reference amount text for Thymosin Alpha-1; this is not a dosing recommendation."
  },
  "peptideContentThymosinAlpha1HalfLife": "~2 horas",
  "@peptideContentThymosinAlpha1HalfLife": {
    "description": "Educational half-life reference for Thymosin Alpha-1.",
    "sourceString": "~2 hours",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational half-life reference for Thymosin Alpha-1."
  },
  "peptideContentThymosinAlpha1Notes": "Se usa en varios mercados internacionales como parte de protocolos de modulación inmunitaria. Se administra típicamente dos veces por semana. La investigación continúa en diversas indicaciones.",
  "@peptideContentThymosinAlpha1Notes": {
    "description": "Neutral educational notes for Thymosin Alpha-1; preserve non-prescriptive framing.",
    "sourceString": "Used in several international markets as part of immune-modulation protocols. Typically administered twice weekly. Research continues in various indications.",
    "sourceDescription": "Neutral educational notes for Thymosin Alpha-1; preserve non-prescriptive framing."
  },
  "peptideContentNadPlusDescription": "El NAD+ (dinucleótido de nicotinamida y adenina) es una coenzima central en el metabolismo energético celular y la reparación del ADN. El NAD+ inyectable y sus precursores (NR, NMN) se estudian en el contexto de la salud mitocondrial y el envejecimiento.",
  "@peptideContentNadPlusDescription": {
    "description": "Educational reference description for NAD+.",
    "sourceString": "NAD+ (nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide) is a coenzyme central to cellular energy metabolism and DNA repair. Injectable NAD+ and its precursors (NR, NMN) are studied in the context of mitochondrial health and ageing.",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational reference description for NAD+."
  },
  "peptideContentNadPlusTypicalDose": "100–500 mg IV o subcutáneo por sesión",
  "@peptideContentNadPlusTypicalDose": {
    "description": "Reference amount text for NAD+; this is not a dosing recommendation.",
    "sourceString": "100–500 mg IV or SubQ per session",
    "sourceDescription": "Reference amount text for NAD+; this is not a dosing recommendation."
  },
  "peptideContentNadPlusHalfLife": "~90 minutos",
  "@peptideContentNadPlusHalfLife": {
    "description": "Educational half-life reference for NAD+.",
    "sourceString": "~90 minutes",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational half-life reference for NAD+."
  },
  "peptideContentNadPlusNotes": "Técnicamente es una coenzima y no un péptido, pero suele agruparse con los protocolos de longevidad. Se recomienda una infusión lenta para minimizar el enrojecimiento y las molestias.",
  "@peptideContentNadPlusNotes": {
    "description": "Neutral educational notes for NAD+; preserve non-prescriptive framing.",
    "sourceString": "Technically a coenzyme rather than a peptide, but commonly grouped with longevity protocols. Slow infusion is recommended to minimise flushing and discomfort.",
    "sourceDescription": "Neutral educational notes for NAD+; preserve non-prescriptive framing."
  },
  "peptideContentSermorelinDescription": "La sermorelina es un análogo sintético de la hormona liberadora de la hormona del crecimiento (GHRH). Se ha utilizado clínicamente como agente diagnóstico de la reserva de hormona del crecimiento y suele mencionarse en entornos de bienestar como péptido de apoyo al eje de la GH.",
  "@peptideContentSermorelinDescription": {
    "description": "Educational reference description for Sermorelin.",
    "sourceString": "Sermorelin is a synthetic analogue of growth hormone-releasing hormone (GHRH). It has been used clinically as a diagnostic agent for growth-hormone reserve and is commonly discussed in wellness settings as a GH-axis support peptide.",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational reference description for Sermorelin."
  },
  "peptideContentSermorelinTypicalDose": "100–300 mcg antes de dormir",
  "@peptideContentSermorelinTypicalDose": {
    "description": "Reference amount text for Sermorelin; this is not a dosing recommendation.",
    "sourceString": "100–300 mcg before bed",
    "sourceDescription": "Reference amount text for Sermorelin; this is not a dosing recommendation."
  },
  "peptideContentSermorelinHalfLife": "~10–20 minutos",
  "@peptideContentSermorelinHalfLife": {
    "description": "Educational half-life reference for Sermorelin.",
    "sourceString": "~10–20 minutes",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational half-life reference for Sermorelin."
  },
  "peptideContentSermorelinNotes": "Se compara a menudo con CJC-1295 sin DAC porque ambos actúan sobre la vía de la GHRH. Su semivida corta hace que la dosis nocturna sea habitual en protocolos no clínicos.",
  "@peptideContentSermorelinNotes": {
    "description": "Neutral educational notes for Sermorelin; preserve non-prescriptive framing.",
    "sourceString": "Often compared with CJC-1295 no-DAC because both act on the GHRH pathway. Short half-life makes evening dosing common in non-clinical protocols.",
    "sourceDescription": "Neutral educational notes for Sermorelin; preserve non-prescriptive framing."
  },
  "peptideContentAod9604Description": "AOD-9604 es un fragmento modificado de la hormona del crecimiento humana, derivado de la región 176–191. Se ha investigado por su señalización metabólica y de lipólisis, pero la evidencia publicada en humanos es limitada y mixta.",
  "@peptideContentAod9604Description": {
    "description": "Educational reference description for AOD-9604.",
    "sourceString": "AOD-9604 is a modified fragment of human growth hormone, derived from the 176–191 region. It has been investigated for metabolic and lipolysis signalling, but published human evidence is limited and mixed.",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational reference description for AOD-9604."
  },
  "peptideContentAod9604TypicalDose": "250–500 mcg al día",
  "@peptideContentAod9604TypicalDose": {
    "description": "Reference amount text for AOD-9604; this is not a dosing recommendation.",
    "sourceString": "250–500 mcg daily",
    "sourceDescription": "Reference amount text for AOD-9604; this is not a dosing recommendation."
  },
  "peptideContentAod9604HalfLife": "~30 minutos",
  "@peptideContentAod9604HalfLife": {
    "description": "Educational half-life reference for AOD-9604.",
    "sourceString": "~30 minutes",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational half-life reference for AOD-9604."
  },
  "peptideContentAod9604Notes": "También llamado fragmento de HGH 176-191 en algunas discusiones. No es un medicamento aprobado para la pérdida de peso; usa un lenguaje de seguimiento neutro y evita garantizar resultados.",
  "@peptideContentAod9604Notes": {
    "description": "Neutral educational notes for AOD-9604; preserve non-prescriptive framing.",
    "sourceString": "Also called HGH fragment 176–191 in some discussions. Not an approved weight-loss drug; use neutral tracking language and avoid outcome guarantees.",
    "sourceDescription": "Neutral educational notes for AOD-9604; preserve non-prescriptive framing."
  },
  "peptideContentKpvDescription": "KPV es una secuencia tripeptídica corta (lisina-prolina-valina) derivada de la hormona estimulante de los alfa-melanocitos. Se menciona en contextos de investigación por su señalización inmunitaria y de la barrera intestinal.",
  "@peptideContentKpvDescription": {
    "description": "Educational reference description for KPV.",
    "sourceString": "KPV is a short tripeptide sequence (lysine-proline-valine) derived from alpha-melanocyte-stimulating hormone. It is discussed in research contexts for immune and gut-barrier signalling.",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational reference description for KPV."
  },
  "peptideContentKpvTypicalDose": "250–500 mcg al día",
  "@peptideContentKpvTypicalDose": {
    "description": "Reference amount text for KPV; this is not a dosing recommendation.",
    "sourceString": "250–500 mcg daily",
    "sourceDescription": "Reference amount text for KPV; this is not a dosing recommendation."
  },
  "peptideContentKpvHalfLife": "No bien establecida",
  "@peptideContentKpvHalfLife": {
    "description": "Educational half-life reference for KPV.",
    "sourceString": "Not well established",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational half-life reference for KPV."
  },
  "peptideContentKpvNotes": "Aparece en discusiones sobre salud intestinal y uso tópico, incluidas combinaciones informales con BPC-157. La evidencia sobre dosificación en humanos es limitada, por lo que los protocolos deben ser conservadores.",
  "@peptideContentKpvNotes": {
    "description": "Neutral educational notes for KPV; preserve non-prescriptive framing.",
    "sourceString": "Appears in gut-health and topical discussions, including informal stacks with BPC-157. Human dosing evidence is limited, so protocols should be conservative.",
    "sourceDescription": "Neutral educational notes for KPV; preserve non-prescriptive framing."
  },
  "peptideContentSs31Description": "SS-31, también conocido como elamipretida, es un tetrapéptido dirigido a la mitocondria estudiado por sus interacciones con la cardiolipina y la función de la membrana mitocondrial. La investigación clínica se ha centrado en enfermedades mitocondriales y cardíacas poco frecuentes.",
  "@peptideContentSs31Description": {
    "description": "Educational reference description for SS-31 (Elamipretide).",
    "sourceString": "SS-31, also known as Elamipretide, is a mitochondria-targeted tetrapeptide studied for interactions with cardiolipin and mitochondrial membrane function. Clinical research has focused on rare mitochondrial and cardiac conditions.",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational reference description for SS-31 (Elamipretide)."
  },
  "peptideContentSs31TypicalDose": "Los protocolos de ensayo varían",
  "@peptideContentSs31TypicalDose": {
    "description": "Reference amount text for SS-31 (Elamipretide); this is not a dosing recommendation.",
    "sourceString": "Trial protocols vary",
    "sourceDescription": "Reference amount text for SS-31 (Elamipretide); this is not a dosing recommendation."
  },
  "peptideContentSs31HalfLife": "~4 horas",
  "@peptideContentSs31HalfLife": {
    "description": "Educational half-life reference for SS-31 (Elamipretide).",
    "sourceString": "~4 hours",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational half-life reference for SS-31 (Elamipretide)."
  },
  "peptideContentSs31Notes": "En fase de investigación en muchos contextos. Los protocolos de la comunidad suelen diferir de las formulaciones de los ensayos clínicos y deben considerarse exclusivamente de investigación.",
  "@peptideContentSs31Notes": {
    "description": "Neutral educational notes for SS-31 (Elamipretide); preserve non-prescriptive framing.",
    "sourceString": "Investigational in many contexts. Community protocols often differ from clinical-trial formulations and should be treated as research-only.",
    "sourceDescription": "Neutral educational notes for SS-31 (Elamipretide); preserve non-prescriptive framing."
  },
  "peptideContentLl37Description": "LL-37 es un péptido antimicrobiano humano de la familia de las catelicidinas implicado en la señalización inmunitaria innata. Se menciona en comunidades de investigación por sus vías de defensa del huésped y respuesta tisular, pero las consideraciones de seguridad son importantes.",
  "@peptideContentLl37Description": {
    "description": "Educational reference description for LL-37.",
    "sourceString": "LL-37 is a human cathelicidin antimicrobial peptide involved in innate immune signalling. It is discussed in research communities for host-defense and tissue-response pathways, but safety considerations are significant.",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational reference description for LL-37."
  },
  "peptideContentLl37TypicalDose": "Los protocolos de investigación varían",
  "@peptideContentLl37TypicalDose": {
    "description": "Reference amount text for LL-37; this is not a dosing recommendation.",
    "sourceString": "Research protocols vary",
    "sourceDescription": "Reference amount text for LL-37; this is not a dosing recommendation."
  },
  "peptideContentLl37HalfLife": "No bien establecida",
  "@peptideContentLl37HalfLife": {
    "description": "Educational half-life reference for LL-37.",
    "sourceString": "Not well established",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational half-life reference for LL-37."
  },
  "peptideContentLl37Notes": "Altamente experimental fuera de la investigación controlada. Dado que los péptidos antimicrobianos pueden afectar la señalización inmunitaria, es importante mantener un enfoque educativo conservador.",
  "@peptideContentLl37Notes": {
    "description": "Neutral educational notes for LL-37; preserve non-prescriptive framing.",
    "sourceString": "Highly experimental outside controlled research. Because antimicrobial peptides can affect immune signalling, conservative educational framing is important.",
    "sourceDescription": "Neutral educational notes for LL-37; preserve non-prescriptive framing."
  },
  "peptideContentDihexaDescription": "La dihexa es un análogo peptídico derivado de la angiotensina IV, activo por vía oral, estudiado en fase preclínica por su señalización del factor de crecimiento de hepatocitos/c-Met y su actividad sinaptogénica. Los datos de seguridad y eficacia en humanos no están establecidos.",
  "@peptideContentDihexaDescription": {
    "description": "Educational reference description for Dihexa.",
    "sourceString": "Dihexa is an orally active angiotensin IV-derived peptide analogue studied preclinically for hepatocyte growth factor/c-Met signalling and synaptogenic activity. Human safety and efficacy data are not established.",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational reference description for Dihexa."
  },
  "peptideContentDihexaTypicalDose": "Solo para investigación; los protocolos varían",
  "@peptideContentDihexaTypicalDose": {
    "description": "Reference amount text for Dihexa; this is not a dosing recommendation.",
    "sourceString": "Research-only; protocols vary",
    "sourceDescription": "Reference amount text for Dihexa; this is not a dosing recommendation."
  },
  "peptideContentDihexaHalfLife": "No bien establecida",
  "@peptideContentDihexaHalfLife": {
    "description": "Educational half-life reference for Dihexa.",
    "sourceString": "Not well established",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational half-life reference for Dihexa."
  },
  "peptideContentDihexaNotes": "Popular en discusiones sobre nootrópicos, pero muy experimental. Trátalo como una entrada de compuesto de investigación y no como un protocolo sugerido.",
  "@peptideContentDihexaNotes": {
    "description": "Neutral educational notes for Dihexa; preserve non-prescriptive framing.",
    "sourceString": "Popular in nootropic discussions but very experimental. Treat as a research compound entry rather than a suggested protocol.",
    "sourceDescription": "Neutral educational notes for Dihexa; preserve non-prescriptive framing."
  },
  "peptideContentGhrp2Description": "GHRP-2 es un péptido sintético liberador de la hormona del crecimiento que actúa como agonista del receptor de grelina. Se ha estudiado por su papel en la secreción de GH, la señalización del apetito y las pruebas endocrinas.",
  "@peptideContentGhrp2Description": {
    "description": "Educational reference description for GHRP-2.",
    "sourceString": "GHRP-2 is a synthetic growth hormone-releasing peptide that acts as a ghrelin receptor agonist. It has been studied for GH secretion, appetite signalling, and endocrine testing.",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational reference description for GHRP-2."
  },
  "peptideContentGhrp2TypicalDose": "100–300 mcg por inyección",
  "@peptideContentGhrp2TypicalDose": {
    "description": "Reference amount text for GHRP-2; this is not a dosing recommendation.",
    "sourceString": "100–300 mcg per injection",
    "sourceDescription": "Reference amount text for GHRP-2; this is not a dosing recommendation."
  },
  "peptideContentGhrp2HalfLife": "~20–30 minutos",
  "@peptideContentGhrp2HalfLife": {
    "description": "Educational half-life reference for GHRP-2.",
    "sourceString": "~20–30 minutes",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational half-life reference for GHRP-2."
  },
  "peptideContentGhrp2Notes": "Se combina a menudo con un análogo de GHRH, como CJC-1295 sin DAC o Sermorelin. Puede afectar al apetito, el cortisol y la prolactina más que Ipamorelin.",
  "@peptideContentGhrp2Notes": {
    "description": "Neutral educational notes for GHRP-2; preserve non-prescriptive framing.",
    "sourceString": "Often paired with a GHRH analogue such as CJC-1295 no-DAC or Sermorelin. It may affect appetite, cortisol, and prolactin more than Ipamorelin.",
    "sourceDescription": "Neutral educational notes for GHRP-2; preserve non-prescriptive framing."
  },
  "peptideContentGhrp6Description": "GHRP-6 es un hexapéptido sintético y agonista del receptor de grelina estudiado por la liberación de hormona del crecimiento y la señalización del apetito. Es uno de los péptidos más antiguos de la familia GHRP.",
  "@peptideContentGhrp6Description": {
    "description": "Educational reference description for GHRP-6.",
    "sourceString": "GHRP-6 is a synthetic hexapeptide and ghrelin receptor agonist studied for growth-hormone release and appetite signalling. It is one of the older peptides in the GHRP family.",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational reference description for GHRP-6."
  },
  "peptideContentGhrp6TypicalDose": "100–300 mcg por inyección",
  "@peptideContentGhrp6TypicalDose": {
    "description": "Reference amount text for GHRP-6; this is not a dosing recommendation.",
    "sourceString": "100–300 mcg per injection",
    "sourceDescription": "Reference amount text for GHRP-6; this is not a dosing recommendation."
  },
  "peptideContentGhrp6HalfLife": "~20–30 minutos",
  "@peptideContentGhrp6HalfLife": {
    "description": "Educational half-life reference for GHRP-6.",
    "sourceString": "~20–30 minutes",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational half-life reference for GHRP-6."
  },
  "peptideContentGhrp6Notes": "El uso en la comunidad suele destacar la estimulación del apetito. Se suelen preferir opciones más selectivas, como Ipamorelin, cuando no se desean efectos sobre el apetito.",
  "@peptideContentGhrp6Notes": {
    "description": "Neutral educational notes for GHRP-6; preserve non-prescriptive framing.",
    "sourceString": "Community use often emphasises appetite stimulation. More selective options such as Ipamorelin are commonly preferred when appetite effects are unwanted.",
    "sourceDescription": "Neutral educational notes for GHRP-6; preserve non-prescriptive framing."
  },
  "peptideContentHexarelinDescription": "La hexarelina es un secretagogo sintético de la hormona del crecimiento y agonista del receptor de grelina estudiado por la liberación de GH y señales de investigación cardiovascular. Generalmente se considera uno de los GHRP más potentes.",
  "@peptideContentHexarelinDescription": {
    "description": "Educational reference description for Hexarelin.",
    "sourceString": "Hexarelin is a synthetic growth hormone secretagogue and ghrelin receptor agonist studied for GH release and cardiovascular research signals. It is generally considered one of the more potent GHRPs.",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational reference description for Hexarelin."
  },
  "peptideContentHexarelinTypicalDose": "100–200 mcg por inyección",
  "@peptideContentHexarelinTypicalDose": {
    "description": "Reference amount text for Hexarelin; this is not a dosing recommendation.",
    "sourceString": "100–200 mcg per injection",
    "sourceDescription": "Reference amount text for Hexarelin; this is not a dosing recommendation."
  },
  "peptideContentHexarelinHalfLife": "~70 minutos",
  "@peptideContentHexarelinHalfLife": {
    "description": "Educational half-life reference for Hexarelin.",
    "sourceString": "~70 minutes",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational half-life reference for Hexarelin."
  },
  "peptideContentHexarelinNotes": "Suele ciclarse de forma más conservadora que Ipamorelin debido a su potencia y a las preocupaciones sobre desensibilización comentadas en comunidades de investigación.",
  "@peptideContentHexarelinNotes": {
    "description": "Neutral educational notes for Hexarelin; preserve non-prescriptive framing.",
    "sourceString": "Often cycled more conservatively than Ipamorelin due to potency and desensitisation concerns discussed in research communities.",
    "sourceDescription": "Neutral educational notes for Hexarelin; preserve non-prescriptive framing."
  },
  "peptideContentIgf1Lr3Description": "IGF-1 LR3 es un análogo modificado del factor de crecimiento insulínico tipo 1 con sustituciones de aminoácidos que reducen la afinidad por las proteínas de unión y prolongan su actividad. Se menciona sobre todo en contextos de rendimiento avanzado e investigación del crecimiento celular.",
  "@peptideContentIgf1Lr3Description": {
    "description": "Educational reference description for IGF-1 LR3.",
    "sourceString": "IGF-1 LR3 is a modified insulin-like growth factor-1 analogue with amino-acid substitutions that reduce binding-protein affinity and extend activity. It is discussed mostly in advanced performance and cell-growth research contexts.",
    "sourceDescription": "Educational reference description for IGF-1 LR3."
  },
  "peptideContentIgf1Lr3TypicalDose": "20–50 mcg al día en protocolos de investigación",
  "@peptideContentIgf1Lr3TypicalDose": {
    "description": "Reference amount text for IGF-1 LR3; this is not a dosing recommendation.",
    "sourceString": "20–50 mcg daily in research protocols",
    "sourceDescription": "Reference amount text for IGF-1 LR3; this is not a dosing recommendation."
  },
  "peptideContentIgf1Lr3HalfLife": "~20–30 horas",
  "@peptideContentIgf1Lr3HalfLife": {
